{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk dominates in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are chosen deterministically based on obstacle direction. Full_rotate is only allowed in a safe, non-obstacle state as a rare scan. All obstacle events force a one-shot turn-recovery state, which returns to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed. No state reached by obstacle events allows forward or random_walk. All uncontrollable events are total in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to model open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, deterministic, coverage-oriented policy: random_walk in clear, short forward pulses, one-shot directed turn recovery, and rare full_rotate only in safe states."
  ],
